// acceptanceCommands.jsonc — ONE frozen -build line per plugin (materialise) and one --rebridge line (debug judge)
// (SPEC-bridgeFramework-v1.md §7.4, §14.1; RULINGS R1, 12:05 #3): the three-run replay protocol holds ONLY under the
// frozen command, because the relationship block carries nodes with embeddings (--vectorize, the embedding cache and
// the hub build are inputs to R1). Every command PINS --decisionStoreFilePath explicitly (RULING 12:05 #3): the store is
// otherwise derived beside the standardsDatabase and a fresh scratch DB per run reads as "no decision block" and mimics
// a replay defect. null-and-honest in B2 — the B3 / B4 builders freeze the lines from their first accepted runs.
// A frozen id compared against a run with a different flag set is a broken test, not a failed gate.
{
	// SHARED TOOL PATHS — not a bridge entry, and every reader of this file distinguishes them by the absence of
	// `standardKey` (the runner and test-runnerContract.js both filter on it).
	//
	// RULING B4R-4 (as amended to option (c), SABLE_RIVER 2026-08-17), on FINDING B4-F9: the sssom-py venv path is
	// DECLARED HERE, ABSOLUTELY, rather than computed by climbing directories from the framework dir. That climb
	// (`path.join(FRAMEWORK_DIR, '..','..','..','..', 'dataStores', …)`) resolves correctly from the main tree and
	// lands on `codeWorktrees/dataStores/…` from a worktree, where nothing exists. test-bgP7.js then took its PROXY
	// branch and reported 44/44 GREEN, telling a reviewer the real validator had passed when it never ran; the
	// sibling suite has the same bug and fails loudly, which is what the difference in accounting looks like.
	//
	// A DECLARED path is what makes the real validator EXPECTED, and that is the whole point: presence-sniffing
	// cannot tell "this machine has no sssom-py" from "my path arithmetic is wrong", and those two want opposite
	// verdicts. With the path declared, an absent binary is UNMEASURED BY NAME instead of a silent downgrade — see
	// apps/graph-builder/test/bridgeAcceptance/sssomValidatorProvenance.js for the rule and its twins.
	//
	// ONE-MACHINE, and said out loud: this is TQ's box. A machine without this venv declares nothing here, and its
	// proxy-only runs are then PERMITTED and labelled rather than pretending to a measurement.
	"sharedToolPaths": {
		"sssomPyBinPath": "/Users/tqwhite/Documents/webdev/educoreForge/system/dataStores/bridgeAcceptance/sssomVenv/bin/sssom"
	},
